  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given an integer NNN.\n\nCount the number of distinct arrays DDD of size NNN containing non-negative integers such that it is possible to construct a graph GGG of NNN nodes with the following constraints:\n\n\nFor each iii (1≤i≤N1 \\leq i \\leq N1≤i≤N), node iii has degree DiD_iDi​ in GGG.\nD1+D2+…+DN=2ND_1 + D_2 + \\ldots + D_N = 2ND1​+D2​+…+DN​=2N.\nGGG is simple, connected, and **bipartite**.\nThis value can be large, so compute it modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nThe first and only line of each test case will contain a single integer NNN - the size of the array DDD.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output on a new line a single integer: the number of distinct arrays DDD satisfying the given conditions, modulo 109+710^9 + 7109+7.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤2⋅1051 \\leq T \\leq 2 \\cdot 10^51≤T≤2⋅105",
      "1≤N≤1061 \\leq N \\leq 10^61≤N≤106",
      "Note that the sum of NNN across all tests is **not bounded.**"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
